     "The same as today",
     "Less than today"
    ],
    "correct": 2
   },
   {
    "id": "q_mf2",
    "domain": "money_fundamentals",
    "text": "You invest €100 at 2% per year and leave the interest in the account. After five years you have:",
    "options": [
     "Exactly €110",
     "More than €110",
     "Less than €110"
    ],
    "correct": 1
   },
   {
    "id": "q_mf3",
    "domain": "money_fundamentals",
    "text": "What is a budget mainly for?",
    "options": [
     "Predicting the stock market",
     "Planning income against spending",
     "Reducing your tax rate"
    ],
    "correct": 1
   },
   {
    "id": "q_cb1",
    "domain": "credit_borrowing",
    "text": "Which figure lets you compare the total yearly cost of two loans?",
    "options": [
     "The nominal interest rate",
     "The effective annual rate (APR)",
     "The monthly instalment"
    ],
    "correct": 1
   },
   {
    "id": "q_cb2",
    "domain": "credit_borrowing",
    "text": "You extend a loan from 12 to 36 months at the same rate. What happens?",
    "options": [
